yer network combining PPI (gene-gene) and miRNA-target (miRNA-gene) edges\n**Step 4.** [ ] Calculate degree centrality for all nodes, identify gene nodes with degree above 90th percentile threshold\n**Step 5.** [ ] Export cross-layer hub genes to `cross_layer_hubs.csv` with required columns\n**Step 6.** [ ] Visualize two-layer integrated network with highlighted hubs, save as `integrated_network.png`\n\n---\n\n", "<class 'langchain_core.messages.tool.ToolMessage'>: Response: \nThis task executed Steps 3, 4, and 5 of the unified multi-layer network analysis plan successfully with no runtime errors. Review methodology: Cross-checked code logic against task requirements, verified input file paths for preprocessed_edges.csv and node_types.csv are valid (confirmed present per provided data description), validated that degree centrality calculation for the undirected network is correct, confirmed filtering of gene type nodes, 90th percentile threshold calculation, and output formatting matches all specified requirements. Confidence score is 100% as all steps align perfectly with requirements and no discrepancies or errors were detected. No modification is required. The code correctly constructs the undirected unified network from the input edge list, computes degree centrality for all nodes, filters gene nodes, selects those with degree centrality >= 90th percentile as cross-layer hubs, and outputs the result with the required columns (node, degree_centrality, type where all type values are 'gene'). No error messages or warnings were detected during execution, input data was complete and valid as verified in previous steps. The output file is located at /mnt/data/lengyang/youjia_project/autoba/BABench/src/promptbio-bench/tasks/a-11-8/result_11/toolsgenie_20260623/cross_layer_hubs.csv in CSV format. Note that Steps 3, 4, and 5 of the original plan were executed together in this single run, no unintended steps were performed. Recommended next action: Proceed to Step 6 of the plan, which involves visualizing the two-layer integrated network with highlighted cross-layer hubs and saving the output as integrated_network.png.\n", "<class 'langchain_core.messages.ai.AIMessage'>: ### Updated Plan\n**Step 1.** [✓] Inspect input PPI network and miRNA-target network files to confirm data structure and column formats\n**Step 2.** [✓] Preprocess edge lists: standardize node naming, assign node type labels (miRNA/gene)\n**Step 3.** [✓] Build unified multi-layer network combining PPI (gene-gene) and miRNA-target (miRNA-gene) edges\n**Step 4.** [✓] Calculate degree centrality for all nodes, identify gene nodes with degree above 90th percentile threshold\n**Step 5.** [✓] Export cross-layer hub genes to `cross_layer_hubs.csv` with required columns\n**Step 6.** [ ] Visualize two-layer integrated network with highlighted hubs, save as `integrated_network.png`\n\n---\n\n\n", "<class 'langchain_core.messages.tool.ToolMessage'>: Response: \nThis task corresponds to Step 6 of the unified multi-layer network analysis plan, which aims to visualize the two-layer integrated network with highlighted cross-layer hubs, completed successfully. Review methodology: Cross-checked code logic against all stated visualization requirements, verified input file paths are valid (all required input files confirmed present per provided data description and previous step outputs), validated that all requirements are satisfied: miRNAs are plotted as orange circles on the top layer, genes as blue circles on the bottom layer, cross-layer hub genes are marked with larger size and red border, all nodes are labeled, visualization is saved at 300 DPI publication quality to the specified path with appropriate legend. Confidence score is 100%, as the code ran without errors and all requirements are fully met with no discrepancies detected. No modification is required. No error messages or warnings were detected during execution. The output file is located at /mnt/data/lengyang/youjia_p